This one tickled me. See what you all think:

Ever been past one of those bad martial arts shops, or seen a small ad
in the back of a magazine selling these really fancy but utterly
impractiacl sword-like objects? Ever played soul caliber or Final
Fantasy XXVII and wondered how they manage to wield those huge, bulky
lumpf of metal so effectively?

Add a new weapon to the game. Uniidentified, it's a "fancy-looking
sword". Identified, it's an "Ornamental sword-like object." It is very
heavy, and takes two-hands to wield. Technically it's a weapon, but not
a very good one. In fact you'd be better off wielding a sling.The clues
to this uselessness are
(a) the fact that it identifies as an "ornamental" object,
(b) you never seem to be able to kill anything with it,
(c) attacking while wielding the thing gives the message "you begin
bashing monsters with your "fancy-looking sword".
(d) if you ever do actually rack up enough damage in it, you realise
that you've been practising the "club" skill.
(e) attempts to polymorph an ornamental sword-like object result in
iron chains. (Sorry.)

Now for the fun bit:

The ornamental sword-like object can be enchanted up to +250 before it
even thinks about evaporating. Yes, you heard me. The problem is, it's
such a poor weapon that each twenty points of enchantment on this
particular item count as only one point. In other words, to get the
equivalent of a +1 enchantment, you need to burn ten scrolls and give
it a +20 enchantment. Also, because it starts so far below normal
weapons in terms of chance to hit and damage dealt, you need to enchant
it very high to make it in any way worthwhile. I had something like
this in mind:

+0 ornamental sword-like object : about as effective as a wielded rock.
+30 ornamental sword-like object : about as effective as a -1 orcish
short sword.
+100 ornamental sword-like object : about as effective as a good katana
or silver saber.
+160 ornamental sword-like object : Might be worth dropping snickersnee
or excalibur.
+220 ornamental sword-like object : Reasonable alternative to
Grayswandir or other high-level artifact.
+256 ornamental sword-like object : Marginally superior to any artifact
weapon it terms of raw damage dealt, but of course you don't get the
special attacks and abilities of the artifacts.

So there you have it. It introduces a new uber-powerful
more-deadly-than-any-artifact weapon, but you need over a hundred ?oEW
to get it, and if you have to resources to get those, well game balance
is no longer an issue, is it?

So why add this to the game?
(1) It would be a great little red herring for unspoiled newbies: "Hey,
I've got this great sword enchanted to +9 but it doesn't seem to be
killing anything. It must be a great weapon though, I must be missing
something. I guess I should keep enchanting it."
(2) People can (if they really want) finally wield a +86 5\/\/0rd of
